      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Welcome ​<user-mention data-id=\"109035\">@Tanet_s</user-mention>, to the community!</p><p>​<user-mention data-id=\"56328\">@Chris21</user-mention> note was correct, but a little brief. I’d like to add that TS33 are not available with AEC, and will not be available with AEC.</p><p>And now here is the result of Chris’s eStore search: the only voltage references currently with AEC are <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/power-management/tl431.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">TL431</a>, <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/power-management/tl1431.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">TL1431</a> and <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/power-management/ts431.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">TS431</a>. You can, of course, also find them via the product website <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/power-management/voltage-references/products.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Voltage References</a>, where you can filter the column <strong>Grade </strong>for <strong>Automotive</strong>.</p><p>Regards<br/>/Peter</p></div>"
